{%- comment -%}
  "More from this brand" slider on the PDP.

  Brands are modelled as collections carrying `custom.type == 'Brand'`, and the
  product's own collection membership is what identifies its brand — see the
  note on the lookup below for why the vendor string cannot be trusted to.

  Renders nothing when the brand has no other products, so a single-product
  brand does not leave an empty heading behind.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- liquid
  # The brand is found through the product's own collections, not by
  # handleizing the vendor. Vendor strings and brand collection handles drift
  # apart constantly in this catalogue: accents fold ("Vontélle Eyewear" lives
  # at vontelle-eyewear), apostrophes vanish ("L'Jai Amor" at ljai-amor),
  # vendors carry suffixes the collection does not ("Abeille Creations (ABL)"
  # at abeille-creations) and some handles simply carry typos
  # (coutney-kelly-books). Every one of those mismatches dropped the slider
  # silently — 19 vendors and 260 products at last count. Membership of a
  # Brand-tagged collection is the fact the store actually maintains.
  assign brand_collection = nil
  for coll in product.collections
    if coll.metafields.custom.type.value == 'Brand'
      assign brand_collection = coll
      break
    endif
  endfor

  # Retained as a fallback for a product that has not been added to its brand
  # collection yet — it is what the lookup used to do on its own.
  unless brand_collection
    assign vendor_handle = product.vendor | handleize
    assign brand_collection = collections[vendor_handle]
  endunless

  # Counted into its own number rather than compared through the collection.
  # A product with no brand collection leaves `products_count` as something
  # that is not a number — and comparing that with `> 1` is a hard Liquid
  # error, not a falsy result.
  #
  # `plus: 0` rather than `default: 0`: default only substitutes for nil, false
  # and empty string, so a non-empty String would pass straight through and
  # fail the comparison anyway. plus coerces anything non-numeric to 0.
  assign brand_products_count = brand_collection.products_count | plus: 0

  # The collection title, not the raw vendor: it is the name the store curates
  # and the one the A–Z brand directory shows.
  assign brand_name = brand_collection.title | default: product.vendor
-%}

{%- comment -%}
  `> 1` because one of the brand's products is the one being viewed — a brand
  with a single product would otherwise render a heading over an empty track.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- if brand_products_count > 1 -%}
  {%- capture brand_heading -%}
    {{- 'products.product.more_from_brand' | t: vendor: brand_name -}}
  {%- endcapture -%}

  {%- render 'product-carousel',
    products: brand_collection.products,
    heading: brand_heading,
    heading_id: 'brand-carousel-heading',
    exclude_id: product.id,
    limit: section.settings.products_to_show,
    cards_desktop: section.settings.cards_desktop,
    cards_mobile: section.settings.cards_mobile,
    overhang: section.settings.overhang
  -%}
{%- endif -%}

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "More from brand",
  "tag": "section",
  "settings": [
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "products_to_show",
      "min": 4,
      "max": 20,
      "step": 1,
      "default": 8,
      "label": "Products to show"
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "cards_desktop",
      "min": 2,
      "max": 5,
      "step": 1,
      "default": 4,
      "label": "Cards in view — desktop"
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "cards_mobile",
      "min": 1,
      "max": 3,
      "step": 1,
      "default": 2,
      "label": "Cards in view — mobile"
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "overhang",
      "min": 40,
      "max": 200,
      "step": 10,
      "default": 60,
      "label": "Peek amount (px)",
      "info": "How much of the next card is visible at the right edge"
    }
  ]
}
{% endschema %}
